# Observation / action contract

This is the interface between RL training and the on-car inference node. If they
disagree, a policy trained in sim behaves differently on the car. It is a single
source of truth with one intentional, fenced duplication. See
[docs/observation_contract.md](docs/observation_contract.md).

When you change the layout, do all three, in one change:

1. Update the Python contract in [libs/f1tenth_contract](libs/f1tenth_contract/)
   (`observation.py` / `action.py`).
2. Update the C++ mirror
   ([observation_layout.hpp](src/common/f1tenth_common/include/f1tenth_common/observation_layout.hpp)).
3. Keep the parity test green
   ([test_obs_parity.cpp](src/common/f1tenth_common/test/test_obs_parity.cpp)).

**Blast-radius checklist** — before changing this shared surface, enumerate and
verify every downstream consumer:

- `training/` (env + trainer) — installs the contract editable.
- `src/racing_rl/` — the observation builder + policy inference nodes.
- The C++ vehicle node via the `f1tenth_common` mirror.

Trace the blast radius while writing the change, not after. A layout change is an
"ask first" change and usually warrants an ADR under [docs/adr/](docs/adr/).
